      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "EDGE\nThis node creates a new shape out of an incoming shape. The output of the shape is the edge of the incoming shape. The thickness of the edge can be regulated by the user.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• Two Pentagon shapes go each into an Edge node that is controlled by a slider.\n• The bottom Pentagon is rotated slightly with the Transform node before going into the Union node.\n• The Union node combines both shapes into a single shape.\n• This is sent to the Shape Render to convert the shape into a texture before sending it out.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 274,
          "width": 850,
          "x": 111.203125,
          "y": 72.9921875
        },
        "class": {
